"><a title="Submit a Tool" href="/submit/" class="btn btn-primary normal-case w-full">Submit a Tool</a></div></div></div></div></nav></div><div class="container mx-auto max-w-2xl px-2 py-8 bg-black shadow-lg"><main class="text-white"><div class="py-8"><div><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="font-mono text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6 max-sm:mb-8 max-sm:leading-relaxed"><a href="/categories/" class="hover:text-tt-green">Categories</a> <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-gray-600 mx-1">/</span>  <span aria-current="page" class="text-gray-600">TUI</span></nav><h1 class="font-sg text-3xl justify-start"><span>TUI Terminal Tools</span></h1><div class="prose text-white mt-5"><p><a class="tt-link" title="Text User Interfaces" href="https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Text-based_user_interface" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Text User Interfaces</a> (TUIs) emerged with early computing era, providing a text based layout, instead of graphical user interfaces (GUIs). They are useful in resource-constrained environments notably in server management, system administration programming, and file management.</p>
<p><br>Even with the advent of graphical interfaces, TUIs still remain relevant, providing efficient, text based user interfaces for professionals and hobbyists and require less processing power where a GUI's overhead would be impractical.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Below is a list of terminal tools that are TUIs.</p></div></div><div class="mt-10"><style>
